{"entity": "CRAG", "type": "method", "description": "CRAG, or the Comprehensive Retrieval Assessment Graph, represents a sophisticated framework designed primarily for evaluating the quality of documents retrieved in relation to queries within the Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) domain. Its core purpose is to provide a structured environment for assessing retrieval performance, particularly in open-domain question answering (ODQA) and knowledge base question answering (KBQA).\n\nCRAG encompasses a structured query dataset that promotes fair comparisons in knowledge graph evaluations. It offers mock APIs to facilitate access to data from underlying mock knowledge graphs. This capability makes it an essential resource for researchers focused on knowledge graph applications and evaluation methodologies.\n\nAdditionally, CRAG serves as a complementary benchmark to STARK, intensifying its relevance in the context of end-to-end retrieval-augmented generation performance assessments. It incorporates default evaluation metrics to measure answer accuracy in hybrid question answering scenarios, thus ensuring rigorous evaluation standards. \n\nThe system is integral to the information retrieval process, directing question routing, web searches, and the extraction of relational data. Within its framework, CRAG also emphasizes the importance of validation and accuracy in entity extraction and knowledge graph application, making it a valuable tool for both academic and practical applications in information retrieval."}
