{"entity": "Adaptive-RAG", "type": "method", "description": "Adaptive-RAG, or Adaptive Retrieval-Augmented Generation, is a novel framework specifically engineered for retrieval-augmented large language models. It dynamically adjusts its strategies for processing queries based on their complexity, allowing for a more refined approach to handling a variety of queries encountered in natural language processing tasks.\n\nThis methodology focuses on improving the operational behavior of large language models by utilizing an oracle classifier, which helps in accurately classifying the complexity of incoming queries. As a result, Adaptive-RAG enhances the effectiveness of question-answering systems. By adapting its retrieval strategies based on the pre-determined complexity of questions, it can optimize both efficiency and accuracy when responding to varied inquiries.\n\nNotably, Adaptive-RAG has demonstrated superior performance in comparison to competing retrieval-augmented generation approaches, effectively balancing the trade-offs between resource management and operational efficacy. This adaptability makes it an essential tool for improving the performance of question-answering tasks, contributing significantly to advancements in retrieval-augmented generation technologies."}
